<BioPage href="dielle/" photoAlt="Dielle De Noon smiling, wearing a white shirt, navy vest and striped tie">
  <p>
    Hello! I'm Dielle De Noon, a board member and the website manager for We Stand 4 Something. I am also the Chair of the
    Delaware Developmental Disabilities Council, which works to improve the laws, systems and services that affect people with
    developmental disabilities and their families across our state.
  </p>
  <p>
    My path began in human services. I earned an associate degree in Human Services from Delaware Technical Community College
    and a bachelor's degree in Behavioral Science from Wilmington University. I then moved into technology, completing a
    bachelor's degree and a master's degree in Cybersecurity and Information Assurance at Western Governors University.
  </p>
  <p>
    Today I work as an Information Security Administrator for the Delaware Department of Technology and Information, where I
    help people get safe, reliable access to state services such as my.delaware.gov. I am also a Digital Forensic Analyst with
    Summit Cyber Forensics. Before that, I supported students and staff at Delaware Technical Community College and wrote
    technology help guides in both English and Spanish.
  </p>
  <p>
    At We Stand 4 Something, I bring these two sides together. I look after our website so that it is accessible, easy to use and
    secure for everyone who visits, including people who use screen readers, larger text or a keyboard. I believe technology
    should open doors for people with disabilities, not close them.
  </p>
  <p>
    I was honored to be named Kent County's Employee Champion of the Year by the Delaware DVR Rehabilitation Council and the
    Division of Vocational Rehabilitation. I hold several industry certifications, including CompTIA Security+, CySA+ and
    PenTest+, and I love working as part of a team and learning something new every day.
  </p>
</BioPage>
